  "chapter": {
    "number": 7,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "A Psalm of David, which he sang to the Lord because of the words of Chusi the",
          {
            "noteId": 12
          },
          "Benjamite."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord my God, in you have I trusted: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lest at any time the enemy seize my soul as a lion, while there is none to ransom, nor to save.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord my God, if I have done this; (if there is unrighteousness in my hands;)",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "if I have requited with evil those who requited me with good; may I then perish empty by means of my enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take it; and let him trample my life on the ground, and lay my glory in the dust. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord, in your wrath; be exalted",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 13
          },
          {
            "text": "in the utmost boundaries of my enemies: awake, O Lord my God, according to the decree which you did command.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the congregation of the nations shall compass you: and for this cause do you return on high.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord shall judge the nations: judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness, and according to my innocence that is in me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Oh let the wickedness of sinners come to an end; and then you shall direct the righteous, O God that search the hearts and reins.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My help is righteous, coming from God who saves the upright in heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God is a righteous judge, and strong, and patient, not inflicting vengeance every day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If you⌃ will not repent, he will furbish his sword; he has bent his bow, and made it ready.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And on it he has fitted the instruments of death; he has completed his arrows for the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 14
          },
          {
            "text": "raging ones.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, he has travailed with unrighteousness, he has conceived trouble, and brought forth iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has opened a pit, and dug it up, and he shall fall into the ditch which he has made.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His trouble shall return on his own head, and his unrighteousness shall come down on his own crown.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give thanks to the Lord according to his righteousness; I will sing to the name of the Lord most high.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 12,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. son of Jemini.",
